Subject: [PATCH] agent: keep the channel on a selection without preferences

A Channel Selection Request whose Channel Preference TLV has no operating
class for the radio's band leaves the choice to the agent. The agent still
pushed a Radio subdoc to OneWifi and moved the radio to
channel_select_configuration_pending, which only a channel change it never
asked for would end. Accept it (the response is unchanged) and keep the
operating channel and the radio's state.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/em/channel/em_channel.cpp
+++ b/src/em/channel/em_channel.cpp
@@ -1986,6 +1986,16 @@
     }
 
 	op_class.freq_band = get_band();
+
+    /* No preference for this radio's band leaves the choice to the agent:
+     * keep the operating channel. Pushing a radio subdoc or waiting for a
+     * channel change that never comes would park the radio in
+     * channel_select_configuration_pending. */
+    if (op_class.num == 0) {
+        em_printfout("Channel Selection Request without preferences for radio %s, keeping its channel",
+            util::mac_to_string(get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str());
+        return 0;
+    }
    
 	get_mgr()->io_process(em_bus_event_type_channel_sel_req, reinterpret_cast<unsigned char *> (&op_class), sizeof(op_class_channel_sel));
     
